                "code": "Example\nWrite \"Banana\" if x is less than 10, otherwise \"Apple\":\n\nfunction Fruit() {\n const x = 5;\n let y = \"Apple\";\n if (x < 10) {\n y = \"Banana\";\n }\n\n return (\n <h1>{y}</h1>\n );\n}\n\nRun \nExample »\n\nOption 2:\nUse ternary expressions instead:\n\nExample\nWrite \"Banana\" if x is less than 10, otherwise \"Apple\":\n\nfunction Fruit() {\n const x = 5;\n return (\n <h1>{(x) < 10 ? \"Banana\" : \"Apple\"}</h1>\n );\n}\n\nRun \nExample »\n\nNote that in order to embed a JavaScript expression inside JSX,\nthe JavaScript must be wrapped with curly braces, {}.\n\nAdvertisement\n -->\n\n ❮ Previous\nNext ❯\n\n ★\n\n +1\n\n Sign in to track progress",
