                "content": "Another way of letting multiple elements have the same styles is to extend existing styled components.\n\nFor example, we can create a PrimaryButton\n and SuccessButton\n that both have the same styles as the Button component,\n but they also have separate background colors:\n\nExample\nimport styled from 'styled-components';\n\nconst Button = styled.button`\n padding: 10px 20px;\n border: none;\n border-radius: 4px;\n color: white;\n cursor: pointer;\n`;\n\nconst PrimaryButton = styled(Button)`\n background-color: #007bff;\n`;\n\nconst SuccessButton = styled(Button)`\n background-color: #28a745;\n`;\n\nfunction App() {\n return (\n <div>\n <PrimaryButton>Primary</PrimaryButton>\n <SuccessButton>Success</SuccessButton>\n </div>\n );\n}\n\nRun Example »",
